CC0 1.0 Universal — Public Domain Dedication
=============================================

The files in this directory (`receipt-vectors.json` and any vector corpora added
here) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

You may copy, modify, distribute and use them, including for commercial
purposes, without asking permission and without attribution.

Why: a conformance corpus that requires a licence to read is not a standard.
The point of these vectors is that anyone can take them and test their own
implementation against ours. If our verifier and yours disagree on these bytes,
that disagreement is the useful product — and it belongs to everyone.

The code that produced them (`attest/`, `attest/web/verify.js`) is licensed
separately under Apache-2.0, as stated in the repository LICENSE file.

Full CC0 text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
